to ask the next question.

2113
02:48:31,536 --> 02:48:32,738
Replace her.

2114
02:48:33,259 --> 02:48:33,879
No.

2115
02:48:34,399 --> 02:48:40,346
Buy a second Pell. A comptroller who cannot ask
questions. A woman who asks where the

2116
02:48:40,366 --> 02:48:43,787
money goes will one day ask where
the bodies are.

2117
02:48:44,307 --> 02:48:45,470
There are no bodies.

2118
02:48:46,991 --> 02:48:47,804
Yet.

2119
02:48:49,823 --> 02:48:55,973
Wesker did not answer that. He drove. And for the
first time, the silence in the car was

2120
02:48:55,993 --> 02:48:59,479
not the silence of a man who had
won the argument.

2121
02:49:01,549 --> 02:49:06,760
That night, in the cold room at the end of the white
corridor, Evelyn Marsh sat on the

2122
02:49:06,780 --> 02:49:12,050
floor in front of the viewing window with her knees
drawn up, and talked to the Tyrant.

2123
02:49:12,620 --> 02:49:18,087
Nobody heard what she said. The four research
associates the Director had bought for her

2124
02:49:18,107 --> 02:49:23,450
that evening worked on in the laboratories without
looking up. They did not get tired,

2125
02:49:23,470 --> 02:49:28,813
and they did not go home, and they did not find it
strange that their new director was

2126
02:49:28,833 --> 02:49:34,113
sitting on the floor of the cold room at three in
the morning, speaking softly to the

2127
02:49:34,133 --> 02:49:34,488
glass.

2128
02:49:35,058 --> 02:49:40,860
After a while she stopped talking. She put her palm
flat against the window, exactly the

2129
02:49:40,880 --> 02:49:45,227
way the Director had done in the basement,
eighteen months before.

2130
02:49:45,798 --> 02:49:50,347
Inside, in the pale mist, the sleeping
thing did not open its eyes.

2131
02:49:50,915 --> 02:49:57,464
But its hand, hanging at its side — its enormous grey
hand — moved. Just once. The fingers

2132
02:49:57,484 --> 02:50:03,010
curled, and uncurled, the way a sleeping
child's hand closes around nothing.

2133
02:50:03,581 --> 02:50:09,961
Evelyn Marsh saw it. She did not tell anyone. She sat
there until the sun came up, a hundred

2134
02:50:28,630 --> 02:50:34,536
In the spring of twenty twenty-eight, Umbrella Life
Sciences had three point two billion

2135
02:50:34,556 --> 02:50:40,462
dollars in the bank, a drug the whole world wanted,
and a problem that money alone could

2136
02:50:40,482 --> 02:50:41,135
not solve.

2137
02:50:41,706 --> 02:50:45,173
It did not have enough people who were
better than everyone else.

2138
02:50:45,742 --> 02:50:47,893
So Albert Wesker went and got them.

2139
02:50:49,262 --> 02:50:55,484
He had a list. Pell had built it — forty names, drawn
