4799
06:34:37,367 --> 06:34:41,952
Crane did not want revenge. He wanted to be
near it. Whatever it was.

4800
06:34:42,641 --> 06:34:44,242
He wants to serve.

4801
06:34:44,764 --> 06:34:48,668
He wants to understand. For a man like
him, it's the same thing.

4802
06:34:50,568 --> 06:34:55,575
I can't tell you what I am. But I can offer you a
job. Umbrella has just acquired half

4803
06:34:55,595 --> 06:35:00,601
the drug-discovery servers on Earth, and it has no
one who understands them as well as

4804
06:35:00,621 --> 06:35:05,569
you do. You'd report to me. You'd have no board.
And you would be close enough, every

4805
06:35:05,589 --> 06:35:08,725
day, to keep trying to model me —
and to keep failing.

4806
06:35:11,245 --> 06:35:17,105
Sebastian Crane stood in the corner office with the
water stain shaped like Florida, and

4807
06:35:17,125 --> 06:35:23,120
laughed. It was a strange laugh — half despair, half
delight — and it went on for a while.

4808
06:35:23,809 --> 06:35:25,069
When do I start?

4809
06:35:27,090 --> 06:35:32,971
It was the third time someone had offered themselves
to him in exactly that way. The Adolf

4810
06:35:32,991 --> 06:35:35,267
half of the mind was keeping count.

4811
06:35:35,837 --> 06:35:41,974
Evelyn Marsh, at a piano: can I help? Sir Martin
Ellery, in front of the glass: when do

4812
06:35:41,994 --> 06:35:48,274
I start? And now a boy who had built a machine to see
God, and seen it, and wanted a desk

4813
06:35:48,294 --> 06:35:48,982
beside it.

4814
06:36:09,024 --> 06:36:14,643
There was one company on Earth that Albert Wesker
could not buy, and it was the only one

4815
06:36:14,663 --> 06:36:16,821
that frightened Catherine Adeyemi.

4816
06:36:17,392 --> 06:36:23,657
Tianhe Genomics was headquartered in Shenzhen, in a
tower of green glass that looked across

4817
06:36:23,677 --> 06:36:29,667
the water at Hong Kong. It had begun, twenty years
before, as a gene-sequencing company

4818
06:36:29,687 --> 06:36:36,022
that sold its services cheaply to hospitals across
China, and it had grown, with the patient

4819
06:36:36,042 --> 06:36:42,515
support of the Chinese state, into something that the
American intelligence services described

4820
06:36:42,535 --> 06:36:49,008
in their classified reports as a national champion, and
that Tianhe's own employees described,

4821
06:36:49,028 --> 06:36:51,633
on their first morning, as the future.

4822
06:36:52,203 --> 06:36:58,608
It had sequenced the genomes of four hundred million
people. It had the largest biological

4823
06:36:58,628 --> 06:37:04,817
database in human history. And it answered, in the
end, not to its shareholders, but to

4824
06:37:04,837 --> 06:37:05,389
Beijing.

4825
06:37:07,458 --> 06:37:11,854
It had also, since twenty thirty-one, been
trying to steal from Umbrella.

4826
06:37:12,425 --> 06:37:18,211
Not with rifles. With patience. Umbrella's Singapore
plant employed four thousand people.

4827
06:37:18,231 --> 06:37:23,757
Nine of them, Hale's people had discovered over
three years, were reporting — through

4828
06:37:23,777 --> 06:37:29,564
relatives, through friends, through a very old and
very careful network — to the Ministry

4829
06:37:29,584 --> 06:37:35,176
of State Security in Beijing. Hale had not removed
