07:00:58,187 --> 07:01:03,830
was to decide what the world felt about Umbrella,
and then to make the world feel it.

5105
07:01:03,850 --> 07:01:09,627
He had a corner office on the tenth floor and a
house on the Brandywine and his student

5106
07:01:09,647 --> 07:01:12,292
loans had been paid off for eight years.

5107
07:01:12,862 --> 07:01:18,284
He had also not slept properly since the ghost
video. He did not tell anyone that.

5108
07:01:20,355 --> 07:01:26,782
The idea was simple. Once a year, Umbrella would bring
its people together — not the executives,

5109
07:01:26,802 --> 07:01:32,557
not the board, not the investors, but the people.
The chemists and the drivers and the

5110
07:01:32,577 --> 07:01:38,534
nurses from the foundation clinics and the security
officers and the families. From every

5111
07:01:38,554 --> 07:01:43,706
country Umbrella worked in. In one place, on
one night, to hear the Director.

5112
07:01:44,276 --> 07:01:50,097
Tomás booked the football stadium in South
Philadelphia for the eleventh of September,

5113
07:01:50,117 --> 07:01:56,210
twenty thirty-five. Sixty-eight thousand seats.
Umbrella flew in twelve thousand employees

5114
07:01:56,230 --> 07:02:02,187
from abroad, and chartered buses for thirty thousand
from the eastern seaboard, and gave

5115
07:02:02,207 --> 07:02:05,651
free tickets to every family
member who wanted one.

5116
07:02:06,220 --> 07:02:07,256
They filled it.

5117
07:02:09,327 --> 07:02:14,779
They came in the late afternoon, in their tens of
thousands, under a clear September sky.

5118
07:02:14,799 --> 07:02:20,312
They came in white coats, some of them, because it was
a joke that had become a tradition.

5119
07:02:20,332 --> 07:02:25,784
They came with their children on their shoulders.
They came in red-and-white scarves that

5120
07:02:25,804 --> 07:02:31,072
Tomás's department had sold at cost, and they waved
them, and filmed each other waving

5121
07:02:31,092 --> 07:02:36,605
them, and posted the films, and the films were
watched, that night, by two hundred million

5122
07:02:36,625 --> 07:02:37,035
people.

5123
07:02:37,606 --> 07:02:43,034
They were happy. That is important. They were not
soldiers or zealots or a mob. They were

5124
07:02:43,054 --> 07:02:48,237
forty-one thousand people who worked for the best
employer in the world, and nineteen

5125
07:02:48,257 --> 07:02:53,439
thousand people who loved them, and they had been
given free tickets to a concert and

5126
07:02:53,459 --> 07:02:58,274
a speech and a light show, and it was a
beautiful evening, and they were happy.

5127
07:02:58,843 --> 07:03:00,775
That is always how it starts.

5128
07:03:02,847 --> 07:03:08,671
In a glass box above the fifty-yard line, Catherine
Adeyemi sat with a glass of wine she

5129
07:03:08,691 --> 07:03:14,317
did not drink, and looked down at the crowd, and
thought about a phone in her handbag

5130
07:03:14,337 --> 07:03:16,309
that she had bought with cash.

5131
07:03:16,879 --> 07:03:23,336
In the press box, among forty journalists who had been
given lanyards and free food, Hannah

5132
07:03:23,356 --> 07:03:29,457
Price sat with her laptop closed and a small, worn
spiral notebook open on the desk in

5133
07:03:29,477 --> 07:03:32,090
front of her, to a page near the end.

5134
07:03:32,660 --> 07:03:38,708
And in the parking lot outside, among the chartered
buses, a man in a plain jacket stood

5135
07:03:38,728 --> 07:03:44,912
by himself, with two private investigators from Oslo,
and listened to the stadium breathe.

5136
07:03:47,482 --> 07:03:51,354
At eight o'clock the lights went down,
and the drones went up.

5137
07:03:51,925 --> 07:03:58,223
Three thousand of them, built by the factory in
Arlington that had once belonged to Aegis

5138
07:03:58,243 --> 07:04:04,825
Dynamics, rising out of the dark behind the stadium in
a single silent cloud, and assembling,

5139
07:04:04,845 --> 07:04:10,859
a thousand feet above sixty thousand upturned
faces, into an umbrella. Red and white.

5140
07:04:10,879 --> 07:04:15,473
Eight segments. Turning slowly, like a
thing seen from far above.

5141
07:04:16,044 --> 07:04:20,524
The stadium roared. It was the first time.
It was only the beginning.

5142
07:04:22,595 --> 07:04:28,071
And then, without anyone telling them to — without an
announcement, without a cue — they

5143
07:04:28,091 --> 07:04:29,070
began to say it.

5144
07:04:29,641 --> 07:04:35,278
It started in the section where the Singapore
families were sitting, and spread, the way

5145
07:04:35,298 --> 07:04:40,808
a wave spreads in a stadium, from section to
section, until sixty thousand people were

5146
07:04:40,828 --> 07:04:44,666
standing in the dark with their right
hands on their chests.

5147
07:04:45,236 --> 07:04:51,041
We are the shelter. We do not wait for the storm. We
make the world safe for those who

5148
07:04:51,061 --> 07:04:56,799
cannot make it safe for themselves. What we learn,
we keep. What we begin, we finish.

5149
07:04:56,819 --> 07:05:01,609
Where we stand, the rain does not fall. We
are not many. We are enough.

5150
07:05:02,979 --> 07:05:04,358
We are Umbrella.

5151
07:05:07,428 --> 07:05:09,800
He walked out into the silence afterwards.

5152
07:05:10,370 --> 07:05:16,747
Alone. No music. No introduction. A single spotlight
on a single microphone in the centre

5153
07:05:16,767 --> 07:05:22,857
of a stage the size of a city block, and a man in a
black suit and sunglasses walking

5154
07:05:22,877 --> 07:05:28,249
toward it, without hurrying, while sixty
thousand people held their breath.

5155
07:05:28,818 --> 07:05:34,539
He had planned to speak for five minutes. It was in
Tomás's schedule. Five minutes, then

5156
07:05:34,559 --> 07:05:37,801
the orchestra, then the fireworks,
then the buses.

5157
07:05:39,991 --> 07:05:40,867
Good evening.

5158
07:05:42,887 --> 07:05:48,844
The roar went on for forty seconds. He let it. He
stood perfectly still at the microphone

5159
07:05:48,864 --> 07:05:55,024
with his hands at his sides, and let it wash over him
and break and die away, and he waited,

5160
07:05:55,044 --> 07:05:59,323
until the silence came back, and then he
waited a little longer.

5161
07:05:59,892 --> 07:06:05,780
Eleven seconds. Somebody in the crowd counted it out
loud. Then others did. By the ninth

5162
07:06:05,800 --> 07:06:11,754
second, the whole stadium was counting, laughing, and
at nine they cheered again, because

5163
07:06:11,774 --> 07:06:15,916
they had all seen the video, and they
were all in on the joke.

5164
07:06:16,486 --> 07:06:21,373
He smiled. He did not usually. The screens
showed it, forty feet high.

5165
07:06:23,563 --> 07:06:29,425
Nine years ago, in a building two hours down the
road from here, there were six people.

5166
07:06:29,445 --> 07:06:35,307
Six. In a building nobody visited, in a company that
was dying, doing work nobody read.

5167
07:06:35,707 --> 07:06:41,430
I told them something, in a break room, on a Friday
afternoon. I told them that every

5168
07:06:41,450 --> 07:06:47,309
great thing that has ever happened in this world
began in a room exactly like that one.

5169
07:06:47,329 --> 07:06:49,134
A room nobody was watching.

5170
07:06:50,734 --> 07:06:51,750
Look around you.

5171
07:06:54,769 --> 07:06:59,985
They looked around. Sixty thousand people, in the
dark, looked at each other. And the

5172
07:07:00,005 --> 07:07:05,406
Director felt it — the new sense, the one he had not
yet bought, the one that the System

5173
07:07:05,426 --> 07:07:10,396
would sell him that night — like the deck of a
great ship tilting under his feet.

5174
07:07:12,587 --> 07:07:17,797
Nobody is watching this room. Not the governments.
Not the newspapers. Not the men in

5175
07:07:17,817 --> 07:07:23,273
glass towers who think they run the world. They are
watching the drones, and the numbers,

5176
07:07:23,293 --> 07:07:26,166
and the share price. They are
not watching you.

5177
07:07:26,565 --> 07:07:27,490
They should be.

5178
07:07:30,010 --> 07:07:31,493
That was where it changed.

5179
07:07:32,063 --> 07:07:38,226
Tomás, in the production booth at the top of the
north stand, would try for years to find

5180
07:07:38,246 --> 07:07:44,549
the exact second on the recording, and would never be
sure. But somewhere in that sentence,

5181
07:07:44,569 --> 07:07:50,733
the rhythm changed. The voice did not get louder. It
got — the only word Tomás ever found

5182
07:07:50,753 --> 07:07:52,053
for it was — older.

5183
07:07:53,743 --> 07:07:57,834
Outside these walls, the world is a storm. You know
it. You feel it every morning when

5184
07:07:57,854 --> 07:08:02,040
you read the news. Governments that cannot build a
bridge in ten years. Parliaments that

5185
07:08:02,060 --> 07:08:06,294
argue while the water rises. Leaders who promise and
forget and promise again. Every year

5186
07:08:06,314 --> 07:08:10,357
the storm is worse, and every year the men who are
supposed to hold the umbrella hold

5187
07:08:10,377 --> 07:08:13,798
it a little lower, and a little lower, until
the rain falls on everyone.

5188
07:08:15,198 --> 07:08:16,095
Not on you.

5189
07:08:17,496 --> 07:08:19,560
Where we stand — the rain does not fall.

5190
07:08:22,080 --> 07:08:27,498
The roar was different this time. Deeper. The
Director could feel it in the stage, in

5191
07:08:27,518 --> 07:08:31,529
the soles of his feet, in his chest,
where the Prototype lived.

5192
07:08:32,099 --> 07:08:37,938
And inside him — in a room on the fourth floor of
an imaginary brick building, behind

5193
07:08:37,958 --> 07:08:44,141
a door with no name — something had stood up, and
walked to the window, and put both hands

5194
07:08:44,161 --> 07:08:45,038
on the glass.

5195
07:08:47,227 --> 07:08:52,211
They will tell you that what we are building is too
big. They will tell you that no company

5196
07:08:52,231 --> 07:08:57,105
should be this strong. They will tell you to be
afraid of us. And I want you to remember,

5197
07:08:57,125 --> 07:09:02,109
when they say it, that they said the same thing about
every good thing that was ever strong

5198
07:09:02,129 --> 07:09:03,484
enough to protect anyone.

5199
07:09:03,883 --> 07:09:04,966
We are not many.

5200
07:09:06,286 --> 07:09:08,700
And sixty thousand people answered him.

5201
07:09:09,271 --> 07:09:10,303
We are enough.

5202
07:09:13,373 --> 07:09:18,828
It began in the lower bowl, behind the stage. Three
syllables. Somebody shouted them,

5203
07:09:18,848 --> 07:09:24,239
and somebody else shouted them back, and then a
whole section, stamping on the beat.

5204
07:09:24,810 --> 07:09:26,158
Um. Brel. La.

5205
07:09:26,728 --> 07:09:32,987
It spread. It went round the stadium like fire
around the rim of a bowl. Um. Brel. La.

5206
07:09:33,007 --> 07:09:39,340
Sixty thousand voices, and a hundred and twenty
thousand feet on concrete, so loud that

5207
07:09:39,360 --> 07:09:45,912
people in the neighbourhoods of South Philadelphia a
mile away came out onto their porches

5208
07:09:45,932 --> 07:09:48,687
to listen. Um. Brel. La. Um. Brel. La.

5209
07:09:52,257 --> 07:09:57,755
He did not stop them. He stood at the microphone,
perfectly still, and let it go on.

5210
07:09:58,325 --> 07:10:00,130
This was the third threshold.

5211
07:10:00,700 --> 07:10:06,849
The first had been a parking lot, and four men, and a
dashcam. The second had been a desert,

5212
07:10:06,869 --> 07:10:12,550
and twelve men, and a thing that walked through
gunfire. This one had no bodies in it

5213
07:10:12,570 --> 07:10:18,518
at all. It was only sixty thousand happy people, on a
beautiful September night, chanting

5214
07:10:18,538 --> 07:10:19,993
the name of a company.

5215
07:10:20,564 --> 07:10:22,942
It was the most dangerous of the three.

5216
07:10:25,632 --> 07:10:26,642
Listen.

5217
07:10:28,043 --> 07:10:29,644
Listen to them.

5218
07:10:32,165 --> 07:10:38,069
The old voice was weeping. There is no other word.
Not with sorrow. With a joy so total

5219
07:10:38,089 --> 07:10:44,062
and so old that it had been waiting a hundred years
to be felt again — since beer halls,

5220
07:10:44,082 --> 07:10:50,055
and torchlit stadiums, and a crowd that had once
followed it over the edge of the world.

5221
07:10:50,624 --> 07:10:56,325
And the Wesker half of the mind, standing at the
microphone with the stadium thundering

5222
07:10:56,345 --> 07:11:01,914
around it, felt something else. Something it had
not expected, and would think about,

5223
07:11:01,934 --> 07:11:03,755
alone, for a very long time.

5224
07:11:04,325 --> 07:11:05,485
It was cold.

5225
07:11:07,676 --> 07:11:08,852
It was too easy.

5226
07:11:09,370 --> 07:11:17,145
It is always easy. That is what no one ever
understands. It is always, always easy.

5227
07:11:17,666 --> 07:11:19,150
That's what frightens me.

5228
07:11:23,300 --> 07:11:28,464
Assessment. Crowd, fanaticism.
Belief, ignited.

5229
07:11:30,684 --> 07:11:31,987
Level sixty.

5230
07:11:34,206 --> 07:11:36,652
New ability. Banner sense.

5231
07:11:42,112 --> 07:11:46,721
He bought it standing at the microphone, while
they chanted, and felt it arrive.

5232
07:11:47,291 --> 07:11:53,146
The stadium was no longer sixty thousand people. It
was one thing. A single great organism,

5233
07:11:53,166 --> 07:11:58,764
breathing, with sixty thousand hearts, and he could
feel every one of them — which were

5234
07:11:58,784 --> 07:12:04,769
burning, which were flickering, which were afraid of
the thing they were feeling and chanting

5235
07:12:04,789 --> 07:12:10,387
anyway. He could feel a nurse from Lagos in section
two-fourteen who would die for him.

5236
07:12:10,407 --> 07:12:16,263
He could feel a chemist from Cambridge in section
one-ten who was chanting because everyone

5237
07:12:16,283 --> 07:12:21,816
else was, and would remember it with shame for the
rest of her life. He could feel the

5238
07:12:21,836 --> 07:12:27,369
woman in the glass box above the fifty-yard line,
not chanting at all, holding a glass

5239
07:12:27,389 --> 07:12:32,857
of wine, and he could feel — like a cold draught
under a door — exactly how close she

5240
07:12:32,877 --> 07:12:33,890
was to breaking.

5241
07:12:36,460 --> 07:12:39,458
The world woke up to the photographs
the next morning.

5242
07:12:40,027 --> 07:12:45,975
Every front page on Earth carried the same image: a
stadium in the dark, sixty thousand

5243
07:12:45,995 --> 07:12:51,873
fists in the air, and three thousand drones in the
shape of an umbrella. The headlines

5244
07:12:51,893 --> 07:12:57,360
were different in every language. In most of
them, they asked the same question.

5245
07:12:57,931 --> 07:12:59,275
Cult, or company?

5246
07:13:01,344 --> 07:13:06,988
In the press box, long after the other journalists
had gone, Hannah Price sat alone with

5247
07:13:07,008 --> 07:13:12,653
Walter Pruitt's notebook open in front of her. She
had read it a hundred times since the

5248
07:13:12,673 --> 07:13:15,936
padded envelope had arrived with
no return address.

5249
07:13:16,508 --> 07:13:22,345
She turned to the last page he had written on. There
was room at the bottom, below his

5250
07:13:22,365 --> 07:13:28,408
blocky capitals. She took out her own pen, and wrote
beneath them, in her own small hand,

5251
07:13:28,428 --> 07:13:31,133
the date, and the place, and four words.

5252
07:13:31,701 --> 07:13:33,639
They're saying it like soldiers.

5253
07:13:35,710 --> 07:13:37,815
Then she underlined it. Twice.

5254
07:13:40,386 --> 07:13:46,477
So ended the conquest of the companies. It had taken
four years. It had cost a great deal

5255
07:13:46,497 --> 07:13:52,314
of money, and one man's mind, and a great many
people's peace. And it had made Albert

5256
07:13:52,334 --> 07:13:58,219
Wesker the master of the most powerful private
institution in the history of the human

5257
07:13:58,239 --> 07:13:58,563
race.

5258
07:14:25,415 --> 07:14:28,820
The narrator is not going to
describe the disease.

5259
07:14:29,390 --> 07:14:34,454
You have lived through one. You remember what it was
to watch a number climb on a screen,

5260
07:14:34,474 --> 07:14:39,594
and to learn the words for things you had never needed
words for, and to stand at a window

5261
07:14:39,614 --> 07:14:44,734
and see a street with nothing in it. You do not need
me to build you another. It is enough

5262
07:14:44,754 --> 07:14:49,703
to say that in the spring of twenty thirty-six a new
illness appeared in nine countries

5263
07:14:49,723 --> 07:14:54,557
in the same week, and that the world's doctors took
one look at the pattern of it and

5264
07:14:54,577 --> 07:14:57,756
understood that it had not come from
anywhere in nature.

5265
07:14:58,325 --> 07:15:05,035
They called it Pale Horse. A journalist chose the name,
from Revelation, in a Sunday newspaper,

5266
07:15:05,055 --> 07:15:09,497
and by the following weekend it was the
only name anybody used.

5267
07:15:11,569 --> 07:15:17,900
What matters, for this story, is what it did to
people. Schools closed in forty countries.

5268
07:15:17,920 --> 07:15:23,899
Borders shut. Two hundred and sixty thousand people
died in seven weeks, most of them

5269
07:15:23,919 --> 07:15:29,192
in the first six, most of them before anyone
had agreed on what to call it.

5270
07:15:29,762 --> 07:15:33,819
And on the eleventh day, Umbrella
announced that it had a vaccine.

5271
07:15:36,389 --> 07:15:43,114
Twenty-two days. From the publication of the first
genetic sequence to a finished, tested,

5272
07:15:43,134 --> 07:15:44,838
manufacturable vaccine.

5273
07:15:45,408 --> 07:15:51,262
The rapid-response platform had been built for the
Pentagon, under Martin Sloane's first

5274
07:15:51,282 --> 07:15:57,403
contract, and paid for by the American taxpayer, and it
had promised nine days and delivered

5275
07:15:57,423 --> 07:16:02,476
eight in a test. This was the first time it had
been used on something real.

5276
07:16:03,045 --> 07:16:08,838
Umbrella gave it away. That was Catherine's idea,
and Tomás's, and it was the correct

5277
07:16:08,858 --> 07:16:14,857
one, and it was also — as Catherine said in the
meeting where it was decided, in a voice

5278
07:16:14,877 --> 07:16:21,080
that made three people look at the table — the single
most profitable decision in corporate

5279
07:16:21,100 --> 07:16:27,030
history. Not one dollar for the vaccine. Cost price,
to every government on Earth, with

5280
07:16:27,050 --> 07:16:32,979
the Umbrella Foundation covering the cost for the
forty poorest countries. Four hundred

5281
07:16:32,999 --> 07:16:39,271
million doses from the plant in Singapore in the first
month, which was exactly the capacity

5282
07:16:39,291 --> 07:16:45,426
that a man had built in twenty twenty-nine and been
asked about by his own chief financial

5283
07:16:45,446 --> 07:16:48,914
officer, and had said: I believe
in being prepared.

5284
07:16:49,483 --> 07:16:55,682
By June it was over. By August the schools were open.
By the autumn of twenty thirty-six,

5285
07:16:55,702 --> 07:17:01,901
in every country on Earth, Umbrella's emblem had
stopped meaning a pharmaceutical company

5286
07:17:01,921 --> 07:17:07,911
and started meaning something closer to what it
looked like: a red-and-white umbrella,

5287
07:17:07,931 --> 07:17:09,727
held over you, in a storm.

5288
07:17:10,297 --> 07:17:16,015
The Umbrella Foundation was given the Nobel Peace
Prize the following year. The Director

5289
07:17:16,035 --> 07:17:21,557
did not attend. He sent Evelyn Marsh, who did not
speak, and stood at the back of the

5290
07:17:21,577 --> 07:17:26,577
photographs, and looked, in every one of them,
as if she were somewhere else.

5291
07:17:29,147 --> 07:17:34,912
He found out in October, five months after it
ended, and he found out by accident.

5292
07:17:35,482 --> 07:17:41,237
It was a shipping record. Not even a real one — an
internal reconciliation, one of the

5293
07:17:41,257 --> 07:17:47,078
thousands that Pell's systems generated every week
and that nobody read. It showed that

5294
07:17:47,098 --> 07:17:52,852
in the autumn of twenty thirty-five, four months
before the first case in Frankfurt, a

5295
07:17:52,872 --> 07:17:58,559
sealed container had gone from the Arklay sublevel
to the Basel vault, and from Basel

5296
07:17:58,579 --> 07:18:04,534
to three laboratories that Umbrella had acquired with
Halvorsen Pike, in three countries.

5297
07:18:05,105 --> 07:18:11,024
The three countries were not random. He looked at them
for a long time. Then he went down.

5298
07:18:13,094 --> 07:18:18,399
She did not pretend. That was the thing he would
remember. He put the page down on the

5299
07:18:18,419 --> 07:18:23,786
bench beside her, and she looked at it, and then she
looked up at him, and her face was

5300
07:18:23,806 --> 07:18:24,714
perfectly calm.

5301
07:18:25,405 --> 07:18:27,642
You weren't supposed to find that
for another year.

5302
07:18:29,662 --> 07:18:30,389
Tell me.

5303
07:18:30,908 --> 07:18:32,120
You'll want to sit down.

5304
07:18:32,641 --> 07:18:33,645
Tell me, Evelyn.

5305
07:18:36,165 --> 07:18:41,149
You built a machine that could make a cure for
anything in eight days, and you sold it

5306
07:18:41,169 --> 07:18:46,212
to the Pentagon, and it sat in a building in
Maryland doing nothing for four years. You

5307
07:18:46,232 --> 07:18:51,158
built a factory for four hundred million doses and
you told Catherine you believed in

5308
07:18:51,178 --> 07:18:56,163
being prepared. You built clinics in forty-one
countries. You built all of it, and you

5309
07:18:56,183 --> 07:18:56,919
were waiting.

5310
07:18:57,319 --> 07:18:58,494
I didn't want to wait.

5311
07:19:00,514 --> 07:19:02,840
Two hundred and sixty thousand people.

5312
07:19:03,360 --> 07:19:03,915
Yes.

5313
07:19:04,436 --> 07:19:05,333
Say the number.

5314
07:19:05,853 --> 07:19:07,817
Two hundred and sixty thousand.

5315
07:19:09,218 --> 07:19:14,221
And forty million a year from frailty and age,
before Aeterna. And nine million a year

5316
07:19:14,241 --> 07:19:19,362
from the diseases we're going to take next, now that
every government on Earth will sign

5317
07:19:19,382 --> 07:19:24,328
anything we put in front of them. I did the
arithmetic, Albert. I did it for nineteen

5318
07:19:24,348 --> 07:19:29,702
months before I did anything else. I am not a monster.
I am the only person in this building

5319
07:19:29,722 --> 07:19:31,163
who has actually counted.

5320
07:19:33,682 --> 07:19:39,409
The Cold-Read gave him her face, and it was the
worst thing it had ever given him. No

5321
07:19:39,429 --> 07:19:45,157
guilt. No fear. No doubt. Only the terrible,
luminous calm of a person who has worked

5322
07:19:45,177 --> 07:19:50,160
something out to the last decimal place and
found that it comes out right.

5323
07:19:50,732 --> 07:19:56,516
He had made her. That was the part he could not put
down. He had found a young woman in

5324
07:19:56,536 --> 07:20:02,521
a dying laboratory who had never once been seen by
anybody, and he had seen her, and shown

5325
07:20:02,541 --> 07:20:08,259
her a sleeping giant behind glass, and given her a
programme with a name, and reported

5326
07:20:08,279 --> 07:20:13,997
to nobody, and told her — over nine years, in a
hundred small ways — that the ordinary

5327
07:20:14,017 --> 07:20:16,333
rules were for the people upstairs.

5328
07:20:16,903 --> 07:20:22,293
She had listened to every word. She had simply gone
further than he had, because she was

5329
07:20:22,313 --> 07:20:25,982
younger, and because she had never had
a bunker to remember.

5330
07:20:28,552 --> 07:20:34,154
The edge of the steel bench bent under his hand. He
did not notice until afterwards.

5331
07:20:34,843 --> 07:20:36,347
You did this without orders.

5332
07:20:36,867 --> 07:20:37,422
Yes.

5333
07:20:37,941 --> 07:20:43,173
Do you understand what that means? Not morally. I
don't care about that. Do you understand

5334
07:20:43,193 --> 07:20:44,807
what it means operationally?

5335
07:20:46,206 --> 07:20:51,266
It means I did not know. For five months, the most
important thing happening on this planet

5336
07:20:51,286 --> 07:20:56,011
was happening inside my own company, and I did not
know. Every government on Earth is

5337
07:20:56,031 --> 07:21:00,868
looking for who made that, Evelyn. They will look
for years. They are better at it than

5338
07:21:00,888 --> 07:21:04,831
you think, and one of them is Wen Shulan,
and she is not going to stop.

5339
07:21:05,352 --> 07:21:06,400
They'll never find it.

5340
07:21:06,918 --> 07:21:12,210
They found the Russians in Nevada. They found the
money in Ireland. They found a smear

5341
07:21:12,230 --> 07:21:17,459
on a dashcam. They find everything eventually. The
only thing that has ever protected

5342
07:21:17,479 --> 07:21:21,905
us is that when they find it, I have already
decided what they will see.

5343
07:21:23,805 --> 07:21:26,639
You have made a fact about me that
I did not choose.

5344
07:21:29,160 --> 07:21:30,633
Let her alone.

5345
07:21:31,153 --> 07:21:32,029
Not now.

5346
07:21:32,549 --> 07:21:38,634
Listen to me. You are angry because she moved
without you. That is the only reason. Not

5347
07:21:38,654 --> 07:21:42,214
the dead. You have never once
cared about the dead.

5348
07:21:42,734 --> 07:21:44,186
I care about the variables.

5349
07:21:44,706 --> 07:21:51,708
She has just handed you the world. Every border on
this planet opened for your aircraft

5350
07:21:51,728 --> 07:21:59,295
this year. Every health ministry signs what your lawyers
write. The Foundation is in forty-one

5351
07:21:59,315 --> 07:22:06,399
countries and the people in them cheer when your
trucks arrive. In one year she has done

5352
07:22:06,419 --> 07:22:10,434
what your contracts would not have
done in twenty.

5353
07:22:10,956 --> 07:22:12,727
At a cost I did not authorise.

5354
07:22:13,247 --> 07:22:19,643
Do you know what I would have given for one officer
like her? One. Someone who understood

5355
07:22:19,663 --> 07:22:25,771
the objective so completely that they did not need
to be told. I had a continent full

5356
07:22:25,791 --> 07:22:27,862
of men who waited to be told.

5357
07:22:29,761 --> 07:22:35,798
She is the most dangerous person in your empire. She
is also the only one who has ever

5358
07:22:35,818 --> 07:22:38,052
surprised you. Do not waste her.

5359
07:22:40,571 --> 07:22:46,267
Wesker stood in the white laboratory for a long time
with his hand on a bent steel bench.

5360
07:22:46,836 --> 07:22:52,277
And the thing that frightened him — the thing he
would take out and look at, alone, in

5361
07:22:52,297 --> 07:22:57,674
the Memory Palace, for years afterwards — was not
what she had done. It was that when

5362
07:22:57,694 --> 07:23:02,056
the old voice finished speaking, he had
found that he agreed with it.

5363
07:23:04,745 --> 07:23:08,708
You will never do anything like this again
without telling me first.

5364
07:23:09,229 --> 07:23:10,276
Is that an order?

5365
07:23:10,794 --> 07:23:13,653
It's the only one I will ever give
you that matters.

5366
07:23:15,673 --> 07:23:16,890
Then I'll tell you first.

5367
07:23:18,412 --> 07:23:24,234
She meant it. That was the tragedy of Evelyn Marsh,
and it took another eighteen years

5368
07:23:24,254 --> 07:23:30,144
to finish. She never lied to him, and she never
disobeyed a direct order, and she never

5369
07:23:30,164 --> 07:23:31,163
once needed to.

5370
07:23:33,733 --> 07:23:39,670
Samira Haddad had been at the World Health
Organization for four years by then. She had

5371
07:23:39,690 --> 07:23:45,627
left the CDC after her suspension, and spent two
years in the field in three countries,

5372
07:23:45,647 --> 07:23:51,789
and been hired in Geneva by a Norwegian assistant
director-general who had read her buried

5373
07:23:51,809 --> 07:23:55,145
report from twenty thirty and
never forgotten it.

5374
07:23:55,715 --> 07:24:01,465
She ran the outbreak-origins unit. It was her job to
find out where Pale Horse had come

5375
07:24:01,485 --> 07:24:05,245
from, and she gave it everything she
had for three years.

5376
07:24:05,815 --> 07:24:11,797
She never proved it. She got close enough that she
stopped sleeping. Fifteen simultaneous

5377
07:24:11,817 --> 07:24:17,733
introductions in twenty countries is not how nature
behaves; nature starts in one place.

5378
07:24:17,753 --> 07:24:23,871
She mapped the eight. She found that all sixteen were
within forty kilometres of a facility

5379
07:24:23,891 --> 07:24:29,604
that Umbrella had acquired with Halvorsen Pike, and
she wrote that down, and then she

5380
07:24:29,624 --> 07:24:35,742
sat and looked at what she had written for a long
time, because she also knew that Umbrella

5381
07:24:35,762 --> 07:24:39,789
had facilities within forty kilometres
of almost everywhere.

5382
07:24:40,358 --> 07:24:46,152
She sent it up anyway. It went to the Director-General,
and then to the Emergency Committee,

5383
07:24:46,172 --> 07:24:51,651
and then into a process, and the process took
thirteen months, and at the end of it the

5384
07:24:51,671 --> 07:24:57,339
World Health Organization published a report which
concluded that the origin of Pale Horse

5385
07:24:57,359 --> 07:25:02,333
could not be determined with available evidence,
and recommended further study.

5386
07:25:02,903 --> 07:25:09,090
Umbrella funded the further study. Nobody found that
strange. Umbrella funded everything

5387
07:25:09,110 --> 07:25:09,655
by then.

5388
07:25:11,725 --> 07:25:17,926
Owen Carrick came to Geneva that winter. He was fifty
now, and he worked for a Norwegian

5389
07:25:17,946 --> 07:25:24,075
foundation that existed, as far as its filings
showed, to fund investigative journalism

5390
07:25:24,095 --> 07:25:25,701
in the public interest.

5391
07:25:26,269 --> 07:25:29,182
They sat on a bench outside the
building in the snow.

5392
07:25:29,873 --> 07:25:35,365
I can't prove it, Owen. I've got six dots and a
company that's within forty kilometres

5393
07:25:35,385 --> 07:25:36,776
of every dot on Earth.

5394
07:25:37,296 --> 07:25:38,168
I know.

5395
07:25:38,687 --> 07:25:43,917
And even if I could — who do I give it to? The
Security Council is four governments that

5396
07:25:43,937 --> 07:25:49,406
need his vaccines and one that needs his money. The
press won't touch it without a document.

5397
07:25:49,426 --> 07:25:50,360
And the public —

5398
07:25:51,762 --> 07:25:57,495
Owen, half the people I work with have a photograph
of their grandmother on a motorcycle.

5399
07:25:57,515 --> 07:25:59,693
Taken last year. She's ninety-one.

5400
07:26:01,712 --> 07:26:02,749
So we wait.

5401
07:26:03,268 --> 07:26:03,952
For what?

5402
07:26:04,472 --> 07:26:10,430
For him to do something he can't explain. He's never
done one yet. But he's getting bigger,

5403
07:26:10,450 --> 07:26:15,027
Samira, and the bigger a thing gets, the
harder it is to stand behind.

5404
07:26:18,177 --> 07:26:21,784
Assessment. Global dependency. Total.

5405
07:26:26,442 --> 07:26:31,039
A hundred and forty-eight governments out of
a hundred and ninety-three.

5406
07:26:31,610 --> 07:26:37,359
He read that line in a dark office, alone, in the
autumn of twenty thirty-six, and did

5407
07:26:37,379 --> 07:26:43,263
not feel triumph. He felt what a man feels when he
comes home and finds that someone has

5408
07:26:43,283 --> 07:26:49,099
tidied his house, and moved everything, and that it
is all in better places than he had

5409
07:26:49,119 --> 07:26:52,454
it, and that he no longer knows
where anything is.

5410
07:26:53,023 --> 07:26:58,330
For nine years he had been the only person in the
world who knew what the next move was.

5411
07:27:15,080 --> 07:27:19,253
Facility available. Oceanic arcology.

5412
07:27:24,019 --> 07:27:29,655
It had been in the Shop for two years. He had looked
at it the way a man looks at a house

5413
07:27:29,675 --> 07:27:33,277
he cannot yet afford, walking past it
on the way to work.

5414
07:27:33,848 --> 07:27:37,070
In the spring of twenty thirty-eight,
he could afford it.

5415
07:27:38,389 --> 07:27:39,831
Purchase confirmed.

5416
07:27:44,314 --> 07:27:48,216
The System asked him for two things.
A place, and a name.

5417
07:27:48,786 --> 07:27:54,851
The place took eleven seconds. Two hundred and forty
nautical miles west of the Azores,

5418
07:27:54,871 --> 07:28:00,866
in international waters, on a shallow seamount that
no nation had ever claimed, at the

5419
07:28:00,886 --> 07:28:05,132
intersection of three of the busiest
shipping lanes on Earth.

5420
07:28:05,703 --> 07:28:07,133
The name took longer.

5421
07:28:07,823 --> 07:28:09,638
Name it for yourself.

5422
07:28:10,158 --> 07:28:10,778
No.

5423
07:28:11,299 --> 07:28:18,470
Every founder in history has named the capital for
himself. Alexandria. Constantinople.

5424
07:28:18,490 --> 07:28:19,876
Saint Petersburg.

5425
07:28:20,395 --> 07:28:26,148
And every one of them told the world exactly what to
hate. Name a city for a man and you

5426
07:28:26,168 --> 07:28:29,035
have given his enemies a target
with a face.

5427
07:28:30,436 --> 07:28:32,933
Besides. There's only one name
it can have.

5428
07:28:34,953 --> 07:28:36,726
Arklay Free Territory.

5429
07:28:37,296 --> 07:28:43,149
It appeared over sixteen months — which is
impossible, and which the world's newspapers

5430
07:28:43,169 --> 07:28:49,292
wrote a great deal about, and for which Umbrella's
engineering division provided a complete

5431
07:28:49,312 --> 07:28:55,098
and entirely convincing explanation involving
modular construction, thirteen shipyards

5432
07:28:55,118 --> 07:29:01,107
in four countries, and a new class of deep-sea
concrete. Every element of the explanation

5433
07:29:01,127 --> 07:29:05,158
was real. Every shipyard existed. Every
contract was public.

5434
07:29:05,727 --> 07:29:11,217
The arcology itself had simply arrived, in the way
that everything from the Shop arrived,

5435
07:29:11,237 --> 07:29:15,489
and the shipyards had been building the
parts that were photographed.

5436
07:29:17,558 --> 07:29:22,295
It was, and remains, the most beautiful
thing Albert Wesker ever built.

5437
07:29:22,866 --> 07:29:29,310
Three concentric rings, four kilometres across,
rising out of the Atlantic like something

5438
07:29:29,330 --> 07:29:35,557
grown rather than made. White terraces stepped down
to the water. Farms under glass on

5439
07:29:35,577 --> 07:29:41,877
the outer ring, feeding a hundred and eighty
thousand people. A harbour that could take

5440
07:29:41,897 --> 07:29:48,342
the largest container ships afloat. Desalination,
geothermal boreholes into the seamount,

5441
07:29:48,362 --> 07:29:54,879
and a fusion-adjacent reactor whose design did not
exist anywhere else on Earth, and which

5442
07:29:54,899 --> 07:30:01,272
the International Atomic Energy Agency was invited to
inspect four times and pronounced,

5443
07:30:01,292 --> 07:30:03,741
each time, safe and unprecedented.

5444
07:30:04,312 --> 07:30:09,959
There were no cars. There were gardens on every
level, and a hospital that took anyone

5445
07:30:09,979 --> 07:30:15,824
who reached it, and schools, and a concert hall, and
six kilometres of beach made of sand

5446
07:30:15,844 --> 07:30:21,557
dredged from the seamount. The apartments were given
to employees by lottery. They were

5447
07:30:21,577 --> 07:30:21,886
free.

5448
07:30:22,456 --> 07:30:28,543
Four hundred thousand people applied to live there in
the first month. Umbrella took fourteen

5449
07:30:28,563 --> 07:30:34,585
thousand, and then twenty thousand more, and by the end
of twenty thirty-nine the population

5450
07:30:34,605 --> 07:30:40,100
was ninety-one thousand, and the waiting list was
two and a half million names long.

5451
07:30:42,670 --> 07:30:46,746
The legal question took four years and
was never really answered.

5452
07:30:47,317 --> 07:30:54,137
Arklay was not a state. Umbrella never claimed it was.
It had no flag at the United Nations,

5453
07:30:54,157 --> 07:31:01,126
no army, no currency of its own, and no citizens — only
residents, who kept whatever passports

5454
07:31:01,146 --> 07:31:07,817
they had arrived with. It was, in the careful language
of Umbrella's forty-page submission

5455
07:31:07,837 --> 07:31:14,509
to the International Maritime Organization, a
privately owned floating structure operating

5456
07:31:14,529 --> 07:31:21,052
in international waters under the flag of a small
Pacific nation that had been very glad

5457
07:31:21,072 --> 07:31:22,911
of the registration fees.

5458
07:31:23,481 --> 07:31:29,558
In practice it was a country. It had a hundred
thousand people, a police force, a court,

5459
07:31:29,578 --> 07:31:35,655
a hospital system, a school system, and a border. It
issued residency, and residency was

5460
07:31:35,675 --> 07:31:41,752
the most valuable document on Earth. And it answered
to precisely one man, who had never

5461
07:31:41,772 --> 07:31:44,039
been elected, and never would be.

5462
07:31:44,609 --> 07:31:50,738
The Security Council debated it in September. Three
of the five permanent members needed

5463
07:31:50,758 --> 07:31:57,097
Umbrella's vaccines. One needed Umbrella's investment.
The fifth was China, and the Chinese

5464
07:31:57,117 --> 07:32:03,386
ambassador, on instructions that had been drafted
personally by a deputy minister of state

5465
07:32:03,406 --> 07:32:09,326
security named Wen Shulan, gave a speech of
exquisite length about the freedom of the

5466
07:32:09,346 --> 07:32:11,212
seas, and proposed a study.

5467
07:32:11,782 --> 07:32:17,989
The study reported in twenty forty-two. By then,
Arklay had a hundred and forty thousand

5468
07:32:18,009 --> 07:32:20,254
residents and its own orchestra.

5469
07:32:22,823 --> 07:32:28,546
There was one problem on Arklay that could not be
solved by design, and it arrived in

5470
07:32:28,566 --> 07:32:30,910
the second year, in a fishing boat.

5471
07:32:31,481 --> 07:32:37,146
Four hundred kilometres of open Atlantic is not a
barrier to people who have decided to

5472
07:32:37,166 --> 07:32:42,765
leave somewhere. By twenty forty, boats had begun to
come — from West Africa, from the

5473
07:32:42,785 --> 07:32:48,777
Canaries, from wherever the storms and the economics
were worst — because the most beautiful

5474
07:32:48,797 --> 07:32:54,658
city in the world was sitting in international waters
and there was a persistent, entirely

5475
07:32:54,678 --> 07:32:57,991
false rumour that anyone who
reached it could stay.

5476
07:32:58,561 --> 07:33:04,893
The first boat had nineteen people on it. The
Umbrella Security Service took them aboard,

5477
07:33:04,913 --> 07:33:11,032
fed them, treated four for dehydration, and held
them in a facility on the fourth ring

5478
07:33:11,052 --> 07:33:15,458
that was clean and well-run and was,
unmistakably, a facility.

5479
07:33:17,527 --> 07:33:20,784
And then the Directorate had to
decide what it was.

5480
07:33:21,354 --> 07:33:27,698
A country would have had a law. Arklay was not a
country. It had no immigration statute,

5481
07:33:27,718 --> 07:33:34,423
because it had no legislature, because its entire legal
existence was a forty-page submission

5482
07:33:34,443 --> 07:33:41,003
to the International Maritime Organization describing
a privately owned floating structure.

5483
07:33:41,573 --> 07:33:47,615
Catherine argued for repatriation with compensation,
because it was defensible. The Security

5484
07:33:47,635 --> 07:33:53,280
Service argued for interception at range, because it
was simple. Evelyn, who was asked

5485
07:33:53,300 --> 07:33:59,210
because she was asked about everything by then, said
that they should be offered residency

5486
07:33:59,230 --> 07:34:05,007
on the same terms as everyone else, and when
Catherine pointed out that this would bring

5487
07:34:05,027 --> 07:34:09,949
four million people to the sea wall within a
decade, Evelyn said: yes. And?

5488
07:34:12,018 --> 07:34:17,993
The Director decided it himself, in nine minutes,
and the policy he wrote has not been

5489
07:34:18,013 --> 07:34:20,083
amended in four hundred years.

5490
07:34:20,774 --> 07:34:25,874
Anyone who reaches the sea wall alive is taken
aboard, treated, fed, and offered passage

5491
07:34:25,894 --> 07:34:31,226
to any port they choose, at our cost, with four
thousand dollars. Anyone who wants residency

5492
07:34:31,246 --> 07:34:36,404
joins the waiting list at the position they would
have had if they had applied from home.

5493
07:34:36,424 --> 07:34:40,594
No exceptions, no queue-jumping, and no boat
is ever turned back at sea.

5494
07:34:41,993 --> 07:34:46,561
And publish it. In full. Everywhere. Including
the part about the waiting list.

5495
07:34:48,580 --> 07:34:54,397
It was the most humane migration policy on Earth in
twenty forty, and it was designed,

5496
07:34:54,417 --> 07:35:00,301
deliberately and explicitly, to be exactly generous
enough that no serious person could

5497
07:35:00,321 --> 07:35:06,205
attack it and exactly strict enough that the boats
would stop coming within four years.

5498
07:35:06,775 --> 07:35:12,350
The boats stopped coming within four years. Two and
a half million people stayed on the

5499
07:35:12,370 --> 07:35:18,008
waiting list instead, in their own countries,
working, applying annually, hoping — which

5500
07:35:18,028 --> 07:35:23,667
was worth more to the Directorate than any of them
could have been as residents, because

5501
07:35:23,687 --> 07:35:26,947
a person on a waiting list is a
person who behaves.

5502
07:35:30,017 --> 07:35:35,613
Catherine Adeyemi came out for the opening of the
concert hall, and stayed for a week,

5503
07:35:35,633 --> 07:35:37,899
and it was the week that broke her.

5504
07:35:38,469 --> 07:35:44,174
It was not the arcology. The arcology was
extraordinary, and she said so publicly, and

5505
07:35:44,194 --> 07:35:50,098
meant it. It was not the schools, which were the best
she had ever seen, or the hospital,

5506
07:35:50,118 --> 07:35:55,957
which took anyone. It was the fourth morning, on the
promenade, at about seven, when she

5507
07:35:55,977 --> 07:35:57,222
went out for a run.

5508
07:35:57,791 --> 07:36:03,717
There were perhaps four hundred people out running.
That was not strange; it was a beautiful

5509
07:36:03,737 --> 07:36:07,659
morning. What was strange was that they
were running in step.

5510
07:36:08,228 --> 07:36:14,081
Nobody had organised it. There was no instructor, no
music, no app. Four hundred people

5511
07:36:14,101 --> 07:36:20,089
of different ages and different countries, out for a
private run at seven in the morning,

5512
07:36:20,109 --> 07:36:25,962
had fallen into the same stride, the way soldiers
do, and were going around the ring of

5513
07:36:25,982 --> 07:36:31,632
the city together in a long loose column, and none
of them appeared to have noticed.

5514
07:36:32,203 --> 07:36:37,530
She stopped running. She stood at the rail with her
hands on her knees and watched them

5515
07:36:37,550 --> 07:36:39,927
go past. And she looked at their faces.

5516
07:36:40,496 --> 07:36:46,092
They were happy. That was the worst of it. They
were perfectly, genuinely happy — the

5517
07:36:46,112 --> 07:36:51,708
loose, uncomplicated happiness of people who have a
good job and a free apartment and

5518
07:36:51,728 --> 07:36:57,587
a school for their children and no rent and no fear,
in the most beautiful city on Earth.

5519
07:36:58,158 --> 07:37:03,191
And their eyes were a little too bright, and they
did not blink quite enough, and there

5520
07:37:03,211 --> 07:37:05,630
were a hundred and forty thousand of them.

5521
07:37:08,201 --> 07:37:13,325
She called Ashcombe that night, from the balcony, on
a phone she had bought in Lisbon.

5522
07:37:14,015 --> 07:37:18,923
Julian, I've been sending you numbers for six years.
Money, subsidiaries, transfers, all

5523
07:37:18,943 --> 07:37:21,332
of it. You've built a picture
out of money.

5524
07:37:21,852 --> 07:37:23,284
A rather good picture.

5525
07:37:23,804 --> 07:37:28,287
It's the wrong picture. The money is the least of
it. The money is the part he lets me

5526
07:37:28,307 --> 07:37:28,496
see.

5527
07:37:30,015 --> 07:37:31,506
Then what should I be looking at?

5528
07:37:33,526 --> 07:37:38,220
(soft) Look at the people, Julian. There are a
hundred and forty thousand people on this

5529
07:37:38,240 --> 07:37:42,933
rock in the middle of the Atlantic, and this morning
four hundred of them went for a run

5530
07:37:42,953 --> 07:37:47,539
in step, and not one of them noticed. There's a
school here where the children say the

5531
07:37:47,559 --> 07:37:52,198
Creed before the pledge to whatever country their
parents came from. Half the residents

5532
07:37:52,218 --> 07:37:56,804
have taken the longevity therapy, and it's free
here, and it isn't free anywhere else,

5533
07:37:56,824 --> 07:38:01,357
and do you understand what that means? It means
nobody ever leaves. It means in forty

5534
07:38:01,377 --> 07:38:05,963
years there will be a hundred and forty thousand
people in the middle of the ocean who

5535
07:38:05,983 --> 07:38:10,783
owe him their lives, literally, in the most exact
possible sense, and who have never voted

5536
07:38:10,803 --> 07:38:11,479
for anything.

5537
07:38:13,500 --> 07:38:14,961
Catherine. Are you safe?

5538
07:38:17,481 --> 07:38:19,405
I genuinely don't know anymore.

5539
07:38:22,424 --> 07:38:25,949
He felt her decide, from four
hundred metres above.

5540
07:38:26,520 --> 07:38:32,188
That was what Banner-Sense did. It had been three
years, and he had learned to read it

5541
07:38:32,208 --> 07:38:38,008
the way a sailor reads water. A hundred and forty
thousand people below him in the dark,

5542
07:38:38,028 --> 07:38:44,292
each one a small steady light — and one of them, in a
hotel on the second ring, was flickering.

5543
07:38:44,861 --> 07:38:48,285
He could have stopped it. It would have
taken a telephone call.

5544
07:38:50,476 --> 07:38:51,821
End it tonight.

5545
07:38:52,342 --> 07:38:52,962
No.

5546
07:38:53,481 --> 07:38:59,600
She is going to destroy you. Not for money. Not for a
rival. For conscience. That is the

5547
07:38:59,620 --> 07:39:02,181
only kind that cannot be bought back.

5548
07:39:02,701 --> 07:39:07,918
I know exactly what she's going to do. She's going to
tell Julian Ashcombe that the money

5549
07:39:07,938 --> 07:39:12,978
is the wrong picture, and Julian Ashcombe is going
to start looking at the people, and

5550
07:39:12,998 --> 07:39:18,039
in about four years he is going to arrive at the
truth, and then he is going to try to

5551
07:39:18,059 --> 07:39:18,510
kill me.

5552
07:39:19,030 --> 07:39:21,078
And you will allow this.

5553
07:39:21,598 --> 07:39:27,075
I'm going to allow it because I want to know what
they do when they finally understand.

5554
07:39:27,095 --> 07:39:32,444
I've spent thirteen years being the only person who
knows what happens next. I'd like

5555
07:39:32,464 --> 07:39:36,550
to be surprised once more before I stop
being surprised for ever.

5556
07:39:38,571 --> 07:39:42,135
That is not a reason. That is boredom.

5557
07:39:43,655 --> 07:39:44,289
Yes.

5558
07:39:46,809 --> 07:39:51,957
It was the most honest thing he had said in nine
years, and it frightened both of them.

5559
07:39:54,528 --> 07:39:59,616
And there was one more thing on Arklay, which
was not in any of the brochures.

5560
07:40:00,185 --> 07:40:06,219
The Umbrella Security Service had existed since
twenty thirty. For most of its life it

5561
07:40:06,239 --> 07:40:12,412
had been what it said it was: corporate security,
twelve thousand guards at four hundred

5562
07:40:12,432 --> 07:40:16,284
sites, most of them retired police
officers in blazers.

5563
07:40:16,853 --> 07:40:22,923
On Arklay it became something else, because on
Arklay there was no other police force,

5564
07:40:22,943 --> 07:40:29,013
and no other coastguard, and no other port
authority. By twenty thirty-nine the U.S.S.

5565
07:40:29,033 --> 07:40:35,244
had nineteen thousand personnel, its own vessels, its
own aircraft, and a rank structure

5566
07:40:35,264 --> 07:40:38,573
that had quietly stopped using
civilian titles.

5567
07:40:39,141 --> 07:40:44,844
Hale commanded it. He had been a security specialist
bought from the Shop for two thousand

5568
07:40:44,864 --> 07:40:50,376
Points in a basement in twenty twenty-six, and he
had never once been promoted, because

5569
07:40:50,396 --> 07:40:55,398
he had never once needed to be. He simply had
more people under him every year.

5570
07:40:55,970 --> 07:41:01,514
Four thousand of the nineteen thousand had come from
the Shop. They stood in the front

5571
07:41:01,534 --> 07:41:07,207
ranks at inspection, and they did not blink, and the
human officers had long ago stopped

5572
07:41:07,227 --> 07:41:11,737
mentioning it, because the ones who
mentioned it did not get promoted.

5573
07:41:14,555 --> 07:41:19,018
Assessment. Territory.
Sovereign in practice.

5574
07:41:24,395 --> 07:41:27,900
Territory. Not facility. Not
asset. Territory.

5575
07:41:28,471 --> 07:41:34,445
It was the first time the System had used that word
since a diner in Wilmington, in twenty

5576
07:41:34,465 --> 07:41:40,174
twenty-six, when a landlord had signed away a
four-storey brick building for two point

5577
07:41:40,194 --> 07:41:41,573
nine million dollars.

5578
07:42:00,632 --> 07:42:05,049
This chapter is about the people. The narrator
has put it off long enough.

5579
07:42:05,618 --> 07:42:11,742
It is easy to tell a story like this from the top —
from boardrooms and stadiums and the

5580
07:42:11,762 --> 07:42:17,955
inside of one extraordinary skull. It is easy because
the top is where the decisions are,

5581
07:42:17,975 --> 07:42:23,959
and decisions make a story move. But an empire is
not made of decisions. It is made of

5582
07:42:23,979 --> 07:42:29,194
a hundred and sixty thousand ordinary
mornings, and the people having them.

5583
07:42:31,265 --> 07:42:36,976
Her name was Mireille Achebe. She was twenty-six,
from Lyon, and she taught the second

5584
07:42:36,996 --> 07:42:42,774
grade at the Third Ring school on Arklay, and she
was one of the happiest people alive.

5585
07:42:43,344 --> 07:42:48,830
She had grown up in a suburb where her mother cleaned
offices at night. She had a degree

5586
07:42:48,850 --> 07:42:54,150
she had been told would never pay for itself. She
had applied to Arklay on a whim, in

5587
07:42:54,170 --> 07:42:59,782
a queue of two and a half million, and been chosen,
and arrived on a ferry at twenty-three

5588
07:42:59,802 --> 07:43:05,289
with one suitcase, and been given a two-bedroom
apartment with a balcony over the water,

5589
07:43:05,309 --> 07:43:06,040
for nothing.

5590
07:43:06,610 --> 07:43:12,123
Her class had nineteen children from seven
countries. The school had a swimming pool,

5591
07:43:12,143 --> 07:43:17,656
a telescope, and a rule that no class could have
more than twenty children in it. She

5592
07:43:17,676 --> 07:43:23,450
was paid four times what she would have earned in
Lyon. Her mother had a residency permit

5593
07:43:23,470 --> 07:43:28,658
and an apartment on the same ring, and had not
cleaned an office in three years.

5594
07:43:30,227 --> 07:43:35,525
At eight o'clock every morning, Mireille's class
said the Creed. She had not been told

5595
07:43:35,545 --> 07:43:40,967
to do it. She had started it herself, in her first
week, because the class next door did

5596
07:43:40,986 --> 07:43:42,822
it and the children had asked.

5597
07:43:43,391 --> 07:43:46,510
We are the shelter. We do not
wait for the storm.

5598
07:43:47,081 --> 07:43:52,390
If you had asked Mireille Achebe whether she
worshipped Albert Wesker, she would have

5599
07:43:52,410 --> 07:43:57,782
laughed at you. She had seen him twice, both times
at a distance. She thought he was a

5600
07:43:57,802 --> 07:44:03,300
strange, cold, brilliant man who had built a city
where her mother did not have to clean

5601
07:44:03,320 --> 07:44:06,372
offices. She did not think about
him much at all.

5602
07:44:06,942 --> 07:44:11,634
If you had asked her whether she would leave Arklay,
she would have looked at you as if

5603
07:44:11,654 --> 07:44:14,396
you had asked whether she would
leave her own body.

5604
07:44:16,966 --> 07:44:23,216
His name was Danilo Ferreira. He was thirty-four,
from São Paulo, and he was a sergeant

5605
07:44:23,236 --> 07:44:25,594
in the Umbrella Security Service.

5606
07:44:26,164 --> 07:44:32,492
He had been a military policeman at home, in a city
where that job meant something complicated,

5607
07:44:32,512 --> 07:44:38,372
and he had left it because of a thing he had been
ordered to do and had done. Arklay was

5608
07:44:38,392 --> 07:44:44,452
a fresh start. On Arklay there was no violent crime to
speak of; his job was lost children,

5609
07:44:44,472 --> 07:44:49,931
drunk engineers, and the occasional journalist
trying to get in on a fishing boat.

5610
07:44:50,502 --> 07:44:56,040
Four of the six officers in his section had come
from the Shop. He did not know that.

5611
07:44:56,060 --> 07:45:01,664
He knew that four of the six were very good at the
job, never complained, never drank,

5612
07:45:01,684 --> 07:45:06,438
never asked for leave, and never quite looked
at him when he made a joke.

5613
07:45:07,008 --> 07:45:13,080
He had tried, once, in his second year, to raise it
with his lieutenant — not as a complaint,

5614
07:45:13,100 --> 07:45:18,976
just as a thing he had noticed. He had said: they're
strange, aren't they, the quiet ones.

5615
07:45:19,544 --> 07:45:25,787
His lieutenant had looked at him for a moment too long,
and said: they're excellent officers,

5616
07:45:25,807 --> 07:45:32,050
Sergeant. And Danilo Ferreira had understood, the way a
man who has been a military policeman

5617
07:45:32,070 --> 07:45:37,976
in a complicated city understands things, that there
was a door in this conversation and

5618
07:45:37,996 --> 07:45:38,918
it was closed.

5619
07:45:39,489 --> 07:45:45,163
He had a wife on the Fourth Ring and a son of six
who wanted to be an oceanographer. He

5620
07:45:45,183 --> 07:45:48,306
never mentioned it again. He was
promoted twice.

5621
07:45:50,876 --> 07:45:56,855
And his name was Tomás Reyes, and by twenty
forty-one he was one of the most powerful

5622
07:45:56,875 --> 07:46:00,526
men on Earth, and he was hollow all
the way through.

5623
07:46:01,096 --> 07:46:06,774
He was thirty-nine. He ran a department of four
thousand people in nine countries. He

5624
07:46:06,794 --> 07:46:12,539
had, without exaggeration, more influence over what
eight billion people believed than

5625
07:46:12,559 --> 07:46:18,305
any single human being in history — more than any
newspaper baron, more than any state

5626
07:46:18,325 --> 07:46:24,070
broadcaster, because he did not own the channels. He
owned the shape of the water they

5627
07:46:24,090 --> 07:46:25,075
flowed through.

5628
07:46:25,645 --> 07:46:31,452
He had done it well. Pale Horse had been his
greatest work: nineteen days from sequence

5629
07:46:31,472 --> 07:46:37,413
to vaccine, and eighteen weeks in which he had taken
the most frightened planet in living

5630
07:46:37,433 --> 07:46:43,239
memory and given it, gently, patiently, a
red-and-white umbrella to look at. People had

5631
07:46:43,259 --> 07:46:47,726
cried at his advertisements. He had won
awards he had not attended.

5632
07:46:49,796 --> 07:46:55,156
At three in the morning, when the building was empty,
he sometimes played the break-room

5633
07:46:55,176 --> 07:46:55,462
clip.

5634
07:46:56,032 --> 07:47:02,113
Twenty seconds, shot on a phone in November twenty
twenty-six, by a twenty-four-year-old

5635
07:47:02,133 --> 07:47:08,075
lab technician who thought he was being funny. Six
frightened people. A man in a black

5636
07:47:08,095 --> 07:47:14,454
shirt saying: every great thing that has ever happened
in this world began in a room exactly

5637
07:47:14,474 --> 07:47:15,424
like this one.

5638
07:47:15,994 --> 07:47:21,434
He had four hundred million views on that file. He
had made it the founding document of

5639
07:47:21,454 --> 07:47:26,955
a civilisation. And he sat in the dark and watched
it, over and over, trying to remember

5640
07:47:26,975 --> 07:47:32,728
what it had felt like the first time, when he had been
a kid with a hundred and six thousand

5641
07:47:32,748 --> 07:47:37,371
dollars of student debt and no idea what he
was standing in the middle of.

5642
07:47:39,561 --> 07:47:41,203
He is exhausted.

5643
07:47:41,724 --> 07:47:44,093
He's the most valuable man in the company.

5644
07:47:44,612 --> 07:47:51,233
Those are not contradictions. I had one like him. A very
clever, very tired man who understood

5645
07:47:51,253 --> 07:47:57,592
crowds better than I did, and who could not stop, and
who in the end took his whole family

5646
07:47:57,612 --> 07:47:58,228
with him.

5647
07:47:58,748 --> 07:48:00,307
Tomás has no family.

5648
07:48:00,827 --> 07:48:04,668
No. He does not. Have you never
wondered why?

5649
07:48:07,188 --> 07:48:13,112
The Director did not answer. But he gave Tomás Reyes
six months' leave the following week,

5650
07:48:13,132 --> 07:48:19,124
with his salary and his stock and his title, and told
him to go somewhere without a screen.

5651
07:48:19,693 --> 07:48:25,810
Tomás went to Patagonia. He came back after nine
days, because he could not sleep there

5652
07:48:25,830 --> 07:48:26,304
either.

5653
07:48:28,874 --> 07:48:35,131
And below all of it — below the schools and the
promenades and the Fourth Ring apartments,

5654
07:48:35,151 --> 07:48:41,407
in the keel of the arcology, two hundred metres
beneath the waterline — was Evelyn Marsh's

5655
07:48:41,427 --> 07:48:42,174
laboratory.

5656
07:48:42,744 --> 07:48:48,942
It had moved from Delaware in twenty thirty-nine.
Arklay Free Territory was in international

5657
07:48:48,962 --> 07:48:54,687
waters, which meant that it was subject to no
nation's law on what might be done in a

5658
07:48:54,707 --> 07:49:00,636
laboratory, and the Progenitor Initiative had
outgrown a sublevel under a brick building

5659
07:49:00,656 --> 07:49:02,799
in Wilmington some years before.

5660
07:49:03,369 --> 07:49:09,018
She was forty-one. She had taken the longevity
therapy at thirty-five, and something else

5661
07:49:09,038 --> 07:49:14,496
at thirty-eight that she had designed herself and
reported to the Director afterwards,

5662
07:49:14,516 --> 07:49:19,911
as agreed, in a memo of four lines. She looked
perhaps thirty. She slept two hours in

5663
07:49:19,931 --> 07:49:25,963
every forty-eight. Her staff of two hundred and
seventeen included sixty humans, who worshipped

5664
07:49:25,983 --> 07:49:31,123
her, and a hundred and fifty-one who had come
from the Shop, and did not need to.

5665
07:49:31,693 --> 07:49:37,289
She had, by then, made ten more of what the System's
panels called Personnel conversion

5666
07:49:37,309 --> 07:49:43,100
— Progenitor (human). Thomas Wyatt had been the first.
The others had all been volunteers,

5667
07:49:43,120 --> 07:49:48,716
and all been dying, and all been told the truth, and
all been given, on the far side of

5668
07:49:48,736 --> 07:49:54,269
it, thirty or forty more years and a brightness in
the eyes and a total, unquestioning

5669
07:49:54,289 --> 07:50:00,144
devotion to the Director that none of them experienced
as devotion at all. They experienced

5670
07:50:00,164 --> 07:50:01,047
it as clarity.

5671
07:50:01,618 --> 07:50:07,696
Three of them sat on the boards of Umbrella
subsidiaries. One was a deputy health minister

5672
07:50:07,716 --> 07:50:13,118
in a country in southern Europe. One was the
chief executive of a shipping line.

5673
07:50:13,688 --> 07:50:19,128
Evelyn kept their files in a cabinet she had made
herself, because she did not trust the

5674
07:50:19,148 --> 07:50:24,588
network, and on the front of the cabinet, in her
small neat handwriting, she had written

5675
07:50:24,608 --> 07:50:25,085
a label.

5676
07:50:25,655 --> 07:50:26,898
The quiet ones.

5677
07:50:29,467 --> 07:50:35,629
Catherine Adeyemi spent three weeks a year on Arklay
after twenty thirty-nine, and hated

5678
07:50:35,649 --> 07:50:41,530
every one of them, and could not have said, in
public, a single specific reason why.

5679
07:50:42,100 --> 07:50:47,708
That was the genius of it. There was nothing to
point at. The city was beautiful. The

5680
07:50:47,728 --> 07:50:53,602
people were happy. The hospital was free and
excellent. Crime was almost nil. The schools

5681
07:50:53,622 --> 07:50:59,430
got children into every university on Earth. Nobody
was forced to stay, and nobody left.

5682
07:50:59,450 --> 07:51:05,522
There was no secret police, because there was no need
for one; the Umbrella Security Service

5683
07:51:05,542 --> 07:51:08,635
spent most of its time returning
lost property.

5684
07:51:09,204 --> 07:51:15,277
She sent Ashcombe fifteen reports in four years. She
could feel, reading them back, how

5685
07:51:15,297 --> 07:51:21,229
they must sound in London: a highly paid chief
financial officer complaining that the

5686
07:51:21,249 --> 07:51:24,031
residents of a utopia were too cheerful.

5687
07:51:24,602 --> 07:51:30,285
In her fourth year she wrote one that was
different. It was three sentences long, and

5688
07:51:30,305 --> 07:51:36,324
she sent it from a boat, on a satellite phone, twenty
miles outside the Territory's water.

5689
07:51:36,894 --> 07:51:43,110
It said: There is no coercion here. There is no
dissent here either. Julian, I have finally

5690
07:51:43,130 --> 07:51:49,278
understood what he is building, and it is not a
company or a country — it is a place where

5691
07:51:49,298 --> 07:51:52,224
nobody has ever needed to be
made to agree.

5692
07:51:54,794 --> 07:52:00,935
He walked the city at night, sometimes, alone, without
security, because there was nothing

5693
07:52:00,955 --> 07:52:06,550
on Arklay that could hurt him and because the
Banner-Sense worked better outdoors.

5694
07:52:07,120 --> 07:52:12,463
A hundred and sixty thousand small steady lights. He
could feel them all. A teacher on

5695
07:52:12,483 --> 07:52:18,138
the Third Ring who had fallen asleep marking. A
sergeant on the Fourth doing a night patrol

5696
07:52:18,158 --> 07:52:23,439
and thinking about his son. Four thousand quiet
ones who burned with a light that was

5697
07:52:23,459 --> 07:52:28,739
not light at all, but something more like a wire.
And two hundred metres down, in the

5698
07:52:28,759 --> 07:52:33,916
keel, a woman who burned so bright that he had
learned not to look directly at her.

5699
07:52:36,106 --> 07:52:41,311
This is what I meant. All those years, in
the car, going home. This.

5700
07:52:41,832 --> 07:52:42,515
I know.

5701
07:52:43,035 --> 07:52:48,796
I could not build it. I had the crowds and the
banners and a continent, and I could not

5702
07:52:48,816 --> 07:52:51,719
build one street like this. Do
you know why?

5703
07:52:53,240 --> 07:52:56,100
Because you gave them an enemy
instead of a roof.

5704
07:52:56,620 --> 07:52:57,585
Yes.

5705
07:52:59,485 --> 07:53:05,241
I gave them someone to hate, because hate is quick,
and I was in a hurry, and I thought

5706
07:53:05,261 --> 07:53:10,885
a people could be held together by what it was
against. And it held. For eight years,

5707
07:53:10,905 --> 07:53:15,998
it held beautifully, and then it burned, and
everything I built went with it.

5708
07:53:16,398 --> 07:53:22,582
You have given them a roof. And a school. And a
doctor. And they will hold for a thousand

5709
07:53:22,602 --> 07:53:23,001
