5710
07:53:25,520 --> 07:53:30,869
The Wesker half of the mind stood on the terrace in
the wind and looked down at the lights.

5711
07:53:31,558 --> 07:53:32,712
Say the rest of it.

5712
07:53:33,232 --> 07:53:39,302
The rest of it is that I was wrong. About all of
it. Not about the goal — never about

5713
07:53:39,322 --> 07:53:45,464
the goal. About the method. Everything I did was too
fast and too loud and too hungry,

5714
07:53:45,484 --> 07:53:51,841
and it cost me the world, and a boy from a Wilmington
laboratory did it better in fifteen

5715
07:53:51,861 --> 07:53:54,922
years with a medicine and a
laminated card.

5716
07:53:57,443 --> 07:54:03,057
It was the first and only time, in twenty-one years,
that the old voice admitted it had

5717
07:54:03,077 --> 07:54:04,741
been wrong about anything.

5718
07:54:05,310 --> 07:54:11,358
And the Wesker half of the mind — who had spent
fifteen years using that voice's failures

5719
07:54:11,378 --> 07:54:17,698
as a whetstone, who had defined himself entirely as the
