6975
09:44:48,195 --> 09:44:54,429
He was eighty years old and looked thirty-five. He had
ruled the human species for twenty-four

6976
09:44:54,449 --> 09:45:00,084
years, and had, in that time, done a very great
deal of good, which the narrator will

6977
09:45:00,104 --> 09:45:04,009
not take away from him, and which does
not cancel anything.

6978
09:45:04,580 --> 09:45:10,106
And he stood at the window and looked out at a sky
that had, four hours earlier, stopped

6979
09:45:10,126 --> 09:45:10,863
being empty.

6980
09:45:13,432 --> 09:45:16,630
There was nobody to say it to.
That was the thing.

6981
09:45:17,201 --> 09:45:22,369
For twenty-one years there had been another voice in
that skull, and it would have had

6982
09:45:22,389 --> 09:45:27,738
